-<section id="wrapper-smoke-test">
-  <h2>Thin-wrapper smoke tests · both directions</h2>
-  <p>The prototype question was narrow: can a native harness keep an external worker visibly nested under a watched child while the child remains a relay rather than a second reasoner? Each direction is exercised from the harness that owns the dispatch — Codex→Claude ran from Codex; Claude→Codex ran from this Claude Code session against the real <code>codex exec</code> CLI.</p>
-
-  <h3>Codex → Claude (<code>claude -p</code>, run from Codex)</h3>
-  <table>
-    <thead><tr><th>Assertion</th><th>Result</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead>
-    <tbody>
-      <tr id="smoke-native-visible"><td>Native child is visible and task-labeled</td><td class="yes"><strong>Pass</strong></td><td><code>external_claude_sonnet_wrapper_smoke</code> appeared as a watched Codex child.</td></tr>
-      <tr id="smoke-bounded-route"><td>External route is bounded and non-interactive</td><td class="yes"><strong>Pass</strong></td><td><code>claude -p --model sonnet</code>, 120 s timeout, stdin closed, no <code>--bare</code>; exit 0, no timeout, empty stderr.</td></tr>
-      <tr id="smoke-raw-relay"><td>Wrapper returns the external result without synthesis</td><td class="yes"><strong>Pass</strong></td><td>Exact four-line marker returned; wrapper reported command lifecycle separately.</td></tr>
-      <tr id="smoke-wrapper-model"><td>Cheapest floor-valid native wrapper model is selected and proven</td><td class="no"><strong>Unproven</strong></td><td>The Codex spawn interface used by this run exposed neither a wrapper-model selector nor the child’s assigned model. The wrapper behavior passed; its floor/cost selection could not be asserted.</td></tr>
