-  <article class="panel warning" id="smoke-conclusion">
-    <h3>Design consequence</h3>
-    <p>Both directions prove native-tree observability, bounded lifecycle, and raw relay. Claude→Codex also proves wrapper-model selection and self-report: <code>codex exec</code> takes <code>-m</code> for the external model and the native Agent tool takes a <code>model</code> parameter for the wrapper. Codex→Claude retains one red acceptance seam because the tested native spawn interface did not expose wrapper-model selection or assignment. Adopt the symmetric wrapper contract with its fail-safe: where native spawn cannot select or report the wrapper model, preserve observability, record the staffing gap, and do not claim floor/cost compliance.</p>
-  </article>
