-<section id="stories">
-  <h2>Stories</h2>
-  <ol>
-    <li id="story-1">As a leaf worker, I want cold machine policy omitted, so that my context is spent on the assigned work.</li>
-    <li id="story-2">As an orchestrator, I want a sharp pointer to the complete active-harness roster, so that routing stays correct without eager context cost.</li>
-    <li id="story-3">As a skill author, I want one public dependency and setup contract with small harness overlays, so that variants cannot drift into unrelated implementations.</li>
-    <li id="story-4">As an auditor, I want declared provider divergence distinguished from accidental copies, so that real drift remains actionable.</li>
-    <li id="story-5">As an image creator, I want image generation routed to a Codex provider and reviewed separately for taste, so that capability and quality gates do not deadlock each other.</li>
-    <li id="story-6">As a task router, I want harness capabilities supplied by named skills/plugins with recorded fallbacks, so that model ranking never invents tool access.</li>
-    <li id="story-7">As an orchestrator, I want every external-harness worker represented by a cheap named native relay, so that the native agent tree shows who is working, on what, and through which route.</li>
-  </ol>
-</section>
