-<section id="decisions">
-  <h2>Key decisions</h2>
-  <ol class="decision-list">
-    <li id="dec-1"><span class="num">D1</span><span><strong>Build <code>until-zero</code>, not an app-shaped skill.</strong> The skill owns domain workflows, deterministic state transitions, projection, and report generation; it does not reproduce every inline-edit interaction.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-2"><span class="num">D2</span><span><strong>Ship a dedicated Runway Capture API with <code>until-zero</code>.</strong> This is not a shared queue and does not alter <code>capture-to-inbox</code>. The skill bundles a small dependency-free server template; setup materializes an editable consumer copy under <code>until-zero/api</code>, following the source/package/instance separation already proven by Capture to Inbox.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-3"><span class="num">D3</span><span><strong>Separate producer and consumer authority.</strong> The Wallet credential can append captures only; a distinct drain credential can list, lease, read, and acknowledge. Query-string tokens are removed, and neither secret is committed.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-10"><span class="num">D10</span><span><strong>Delegate Shortcut authoring to the external Shortcuts Playground skill.</strong> <code>until-zero setup</code> discloses the declared name, kind, source, version, and capability and obtains explicit consent, then asks Shortcuts Playground to build, validate, archive, sign, and verify a minimal “Capture to Runway” Shortcut. The generated Shortcut accepts Transaction input and uses import questions for the dedicated API URL and append-only producer token, so no secret is committed. Setup then guides the user through the Apple-owned step it cannot perform: import the Shortcut, create a personal <em>Transaction</em> automation, select cards, choose <em>Run Immediately</em>, and run the generated Shortcut with the transaction as input.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-11"><span class="num">D11</span><span><strong>Make Railway the default deployment path, with an effect-verified guided fallback.</strong> Setup first materializes the API locally. If the Railway CLI is installed and authenticated, it offers to create or reuse the project, service, persistent volume, and secrets, deploys from the consumer-owned copy, waits for completion, and verifies health plus authentication boundaries. If the CLI or authentication is missing, setup gives exact Railway steps, records the incomplete gate, and resumes at verification after the user finishes. It never fabricates provider state or store secrets in <code>deployment.json</code>.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-4"><span class="num">D4</span><span><strong>Keep canonical financial state readable and local.</strong> Accounts, rules, events, FX, transactions, pending captures, and audit/approval records live in the consumer instance as versioned JSON/JSONL with atomic writes and a single-writer lock.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-5"><span class="num">D5</span><span><strong>Port the engine to stdlib Python.</strong> Skill-repo conventions prohibit a new dependency stack; parity is established against the existing TypeScript oracle before the port becomes authoritative.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-6"><span class="num">D6</span><span><strong>Mapped captures count; unmapped captures do not.</strong> A Wallet charge mapped deterministically to a known account enters as <code>uncleared</code>. Ambiguous captures remain pending and excluded, fixing the current model/comment disagreement.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-7"><span class="num">D7</span><span><strong>Review changes, not raw state.</strong> Reconciliations and material model edits become hash-addressed proposed change sets. Each proposal embeds exact before/after runway effects at an explicit date; approval is recorded before apply.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-8"><span class="num">D8</span><span><strong>Keep orchestration one-way.</strong> <code>until-zero</code> is standalone and carries no control-plane reference. The control plane may optionally invoke it by name; when configured, refresh runs before the morning brief and failures do not block unrelated inbox/task phases.</span></li>
-    <li id="dec-9"><span class="num">D9</span><span><strong>Keep migration out of the skill.</strong> The package contains no Lakebed exporter, importer, retirement route, or real data. Once the skill is installed in its actual consumer workspace, a separate one-time job generates a secret-safe dump, imports the selected owner through ordinary proposals, proves parity, and records rollback evidence before Lakebed is disabled.</span></li>
-  </ol>
-</section>
-
-<section id="migration">
-  <h2>One-time post-install cutover</h2>
-  <p class="section-intro">This sequence is operational work after the reusable skill is merged and installed. None of its dump, transformation, import, dual-run, or retirement machinery ships in <code>until-zero</code>.</p>
-  <div class="phases">
-    <article class="phase" id="phase-0"><span class="phase-no">0 · INSTALL</span><h3>Materialize the real consumer</h3><p>Merge the skill PR, install it in the actual working directory, materialize the instance, and verify its deterministic core before touching live data.</p><p class="gate"><strong>Gate:</strong> package tests pass and the installed empty instance validates structurally.</p></article>
-    <article class="phase" id="phase-1"><span class="phase-no">1 · DUMP</span><h3>Generate a secret-safe export</h3><p>As a one-time job, export every domain table, preserve IDs and links, explicitly select the intended owner, exclude tokens and credentials, and record counts plus source hash.</p><p class="gate"><strong>Gate:</strong> both settings scopes are dispositioned, counts reconcile, and a secret scan is clean.</p></article>
-    <article class="phase" id="phase-2"><span class="phase-no">2 · IMPORT</span><h3>Transform through reviewed proposals</h3><p>Normalize the selected owner into the installed state contract, show exact before/after projections, approve the bound proposal hashes, and apply only to the consumer instance.</p><p class="gate"><strong>Gate:</strong> canonical state validates and frozen-date real-data output matches the legacy oracle.</p></article>
-    <article class="phase" id="phase-3"><span class="phase-no">3 · LIVE VERIFY</span><h3>Prove capture and statement flow</h3><p>Deploy the dedicated API, build the Shortcut, complete one live Wallet capture and one statement reconciliation, and compare missing/duplicate capture, account mapping, card timing, and zero dates while Lakebed remains readable.</p><p class="gate"><strong>Gate:</strong> no unexplained drift and rollback is rehearsed.</p></article>
-    <article class="phase" id="phase-4"><span class="phase-no">4 · RETIRE</span><h3>Disable old runtime, retain evidence</h3><p>Disable old Shortcut and tokens, archive the dump and Lakebed implementation, and retain links to the skill, instance, deployment, reports, cutover evidence, and rollback record.</p><p class="gate"><strong>Gate:</strong> post-retirement refresh/report smoke passes.</p></article>
-  </div>
-</section>
-
-<section id="criteria">
-  <h2>Definition of done</h2>
-  <ul class="criteria">
-    <li id="ac-1" data-criterion>The intended Lakebed owner is explicitly selected from the two settings scopes; an export contains all domain rows for that owner and exposes no token value.<small>Check: sanitized manifest, counts, and secret scan.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-2" data-criterion>The Python projection matches the TypeScript oracle for all 27 existing assertions on identical frozen dates.<small>Check: cross-engine fixture runner.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-3" data-criterion>The imported real dataset produces the same opening balance, three zero dates, next statement totals/dates, and ordered timeline under both engines.<small>Check: normalized snapshot diff.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-4" data-criterion>The dedicated Runway Capture API accepts only the versioned Wallet transaction envelope, exposes oldest-first paginated draining, and rejects unrelated capture shapes.<small>Check: positive/negative API contract tests with more than one page.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-5" data-criterion>The Wallet producer credential can append but cannot list, lease, read, acknowledge, or administer captures; the separate drain credential passes those consumer operations.<small>Check: negative authorization matrix.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-6" data-criterion>Two concurrent drain attempts cannot apply the same capture twice; a failed local write leaves the remote item unacknowledged.<small>Check: lease race and fault-injection tests.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-7" data-criterion>A mapped Wallet charge is stored once as uncleared and changes the runway through its account’s correct cash/card timing.<small>Check: live Shortcut-shaped capture and projection diff.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-8" data-criterion>An unmapped Wallet charge remains pending, is visible in the review surface, and does not affect any zero date until assigned.<small>Check: unmapped fixture before/after assignment.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-9" data-criterion>A statement import deterministically proposes unique matches, balance changes, and new transactions while leaving ambiguous rows unresolved and canonical state unchanged; recurring rules are separate edits.<small>Check: hash canonical files before/after change generation.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-10" data-criterion>Applying a proposal requires an approval whose content hash matches; stale or altered proposals are rejected and leave state unchanged.<small>Check: approve, tamper, and stale-hash tests.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-11" data-criterion>The generated <code>current.html</code> is self-contained, responsive, readable in light/dark modes, and shows runway, pending decisions, assumptions, and provenance; each proposal separately embeds its exact before/after effects.<small>Check: offline render plus proposal-content inspection.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-12" data-criterion>Every applied mutation records timestamp, actor, source capture/proposal IDs, before/after hashes, and approval ID without embedding secrets.<small>Check: audit-log schema and secret scan.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-13" data-criterion>Setup and upgrade preserve consumer-edited instance files, emit adjacent candidates for conflicts, and do not overwrite financial state or deployment identity.<small>Check: fresh, idempotent, edited-instance evals.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-14" data-criterion>A configured morning control-plane run refreshes runway capture and includes a concise status/link; an unavailable runway phase is reported while later workspace phases continue.<small>Check: healthy and failure-path orchestrator probes.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-15" data-criterion>The existing <code>capture-to-inbox</code> skill, consumer instance, Railway service, and share-sheet flow remain unchanged by the runway migration.<small>Check: zero-diff inventory plus its existing end-to-end smoke test.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-16" data-criterion>The old Lakebed runtime is disabled only after a completed dual-run window includes at least one live Wallet capture and one statement reconciliation with a rehearsed rollback.<small>Check: signed cutover checklist and evidence links.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-17" data-criterion>The Until Zero Project note remains the known home and links the canonical skill, consumer instance, active report, deployment, export, and archived repo.<small>Check: workspace link lint and manual navigation.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-18" data-criterion><code>until-zero</code> declares Shortcuts Playground as an external capability with exact identity, source, version, and capability disclosure, and setup obtains explicit consent before installing or invoking it.<small>Check: clean-project setup probe with absent and present dependency.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-19" data-criterion>On first-run setup, Shortcuts Playground produces validator-clean unsigned XML, archives it, signs an importable <code>.shortcut</code>, and verifies the signed file exists with non-zero size; committed artifacts contain placeholders/import questions rather than a producer token.<small>Check: plugin pipeline transcript, artifact inspection, and secret scan.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-20" data-criterion>A new user can follow the generated setup guide to import the Shortcut, create an iOS Transaction automation for selected cards, set it to Run Immediately, pass Transaction input to the Shortcut, and deliver one live capture to their dedicated Runway Capture API.<small>Check: clean-phone setup walkthrough and resulting Queue ID.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-21" data-criterion>When the Railway CLI is installed and authenticated, setup can create or reuse the project, service, persistent volume, environment variables, and domain; deploy the consumer-owned API source; and verify healthy/authenticated behavior without exposing a secret.<small>Check: effect-verified setup in a disposable Railway fixture, followed by teardown.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-22" data-criterion>When the Railway CLI or login is unavailable, setup stops before mutation, prints exact dashboard/CLI steps for every missing resource and secret, records the pending gate, and resumes with the same verification checks after the user completes them.<small>Check: clean environment with Railway absent and present-but-logged-out.</small></li>
-    <li id="ac-23" data-criterion>Fresh and repeated setup runs preserve the dedicated deployment identity, queue data, Shortcut artifacts, financial state, and consumer-edited API files while advancing untouched template files or emitting adjacent setup candidates.<small>Check: fresh, byte-identical rerun, edited-file upgrade, and existing-deployment evals.</small></li>
-  </ul>
-</section>
-
-<section id="checks">
-  <h2>How it will be checked</h2>
-  <div class="check-grid">
-    <article class="check" id="check-engine"><h3>Projection seam</h3><p>Cross-engine golden runner on synthetic edge cases and one sanitized production snapshot, with date fixed and amounts compared in integer minor units.</p></article>
-    <article class="check" id="check-capture"><h3>Capture seam</h3><p>Dependency-free dedicated-API tests plus both Railway setup branches, live health/auth, Shortcut-shaped post, lease/drain, local commit, ack, replay, and upgrade reconciliation.</p></article>
-    <article class="check" id="check-skill"><h3>Skill seam</h3><p>Fresh-agent probes for runway query, natural-language rule edit, unmapped transaction, statement proposal, stale approval, and resume after interruption.</p></article>
-    <article class="check" id="check-surface"><h3>Human seam</h3><p>Offline render and browser screenshots at phone/desktop sizes; keyboard navigation, WCAG contrast, and human approval of the real current report.</p></article>
-    <article class="check" id="check-shortcut"><h3>Shortcut seam</h3><p>External dependency consent, Shortcuts Playground validation/signing evidence, non-secret artifact inspection, clean import, personal Transaction automation setup, and one live capture from iPhone.</p></article>
-  </div>
-  <p class="note" id="unchecked">Deliberately unchecked until the one-time cutover: prediction accuracy beyond the encoded assumptions. Parity proves semantic equivalence and provenance, not that future cashflow assumptions are objectively correct.</p>
-</section>
-
-<section id="assumptions">
-  <h2>Assumptions to validate</h2>
-  <table>
-    <thead><tr><th>Hypothesis</th><th>Cheapest falsification</th><th>Blocks</th></tr></thead>
-    <tbody>
-      <tr class="assumption" id="assumption-1"><td><strong>The intended owner can be exported completely.</strong></td><td>Sanitized dump grouped by owner; compare counts and linked IDs.</td><td>Any import or retirement.</td></tr>
-      <tr class="assumption" id="assumption-2"><td><strong>Python can reproduce every engine edge.</strong></td><td>Port only the 27 oracle fixtures first and compare normalized output.</td><td>Runway skill build.</td></tr>
-      <tr class="assumption" id="assumption-3"><td><strong>A small dedicated service can be provisioned or resumed reliably from setup.</strong></td><td>Materialize the template in a clean fixture, exercise authenticated Railway CLI creation in a disposable service, then repeat with the CLI absent and logged out.</td><td>Shortcut generation and Wallet cutover.</td></tr>
-      <tr class="assumption" id="assumption-4"><td><strong>A review-first interaction is sufficient.</strong></td><td>Use a generated report for one real statement reconciliation before deleting any app editing path.</td><td>Lakebed UI retirement.</td></tr>
-      <tr class="assumption" id="assumption-5"><td><strong>A standalone Shortcut can receive Apple’s Transaction input reliably across the target iOS version.</strong></td><td>Have Shortcuts Playground build and sign the smallest POST workflow, then wire it to a personal Transaction automation on the user’s phone.</td><td>Wallet cutover and removal of manual authoring instructions.</td></tr>
-    </tbody>
-  </table>
-</section>
-
-<details id="risks" open>
-  <summary>Risks and mitigations</summary>
-  <ul class="risk-list">
-    <li id="risk-1"><strong>Silent financial drift.</strong> Freeze dates, retain minor units, compare normalized outputs, and block cutover on any unexplained delta.</li>
-    <li id="risk-2"><strong>Wrong-owner migration.</strong> Require explicit owner selection and manifest review; never infer from row order or merge scopes.</li>
-    <li id="risk-3"><strong>Dedicated-service setup fails halfway.</strong> Record each effect-verified gate, reuse healthy Railway resources on resume, never overwrite deployment identity, acknowledge only after local commit, and keep Lakebed capture live until the new endpoint passes a phone smoke test.</li>
-    <li id="risk-4"><strong>Second source of truth in HTML.</strong> Generate from canonical state and proposals; browser controls annotate/approve only and never directly edit financial records.</li>
-    <li id="risk-5"><strong>Over-scoped first release.</strong> Defer rich ledger editing, automatic FX, and broad analytics; ship query, capture, proposals, reconciliation, and review first.</li>
-    <li id="risk-6"><strong>Sensitive raw history spreads into the workspace.</strong> Redact tokens, make raw-log import opt-in, set retention, and keep financial capture outside the general Inbox.</li>
-    <li id="risk-7"><strong>The external Shortcut capability is unavailable or changes.</strong> Pin and record the reviewed plugin version, stop only the Shortcut setup phase with an exact remediation, preserve already-generated consumer artifacts, and retain the documented manual wiring path as a disclosed fallback rather than silently inventing plist actions.</li>
-  </ul>
-</details>
-
-<details id="required">
-  <summary>Required implementation evidence</summary>
-  <ul class="risk-list">
-    <li id="req-1">Post-install one-time cutover record: sanitized dump manifest, owner selection, counts, source hash, and secret scan.</li>
-    <li id="req-2">Post-import parity report keyed to frozen date and fixture hash; these artifacts remain outside the reusable skill.</li>
-    <li id="req-3">Dedicated Capture API authorization, concurrency, failure, template-upgrade, and automatic/guided Railway setup results.</li>
-    <li id="req-4">Probe transcripts and pass/fail table for the new skill.</li>
-    <li id="req-5">Desktop/mobile review-surface screenshots and contrast results.</li>
-    <li id="req-6">Dual-run ledger, Shortcut repoint proof, rollback rehearsal, and retirement checklist.</li>
-    <li id="req-7">Shortcuts Playground provenance/consent record, validator and signer output, artifact hashes, setup guide, and live iPhone Queue ID.</li>
-  </ul>
-</details>
-
-<details id="out-of-scope">
-  <summary>Out of scope for this migration</summary>
-  <ul class="risk-list">
-    <li id="oos-1">Rebuilding the full spreadsheet-grid editor in HTML.</li>
-    <li id="oos-2">Bank aggregation, investment tracking, envelopes/budgets, or multi-user collaboration.</li>
-    <li id="oos-3">Changing the pay-in-full card model or redefining certainty bands beyond the explicit unmapped-transaction fix.</li>
-    <li id="oos-4">Automatic server-side FX refresh until capture and migration are proven.</li>
-    <li id="oos-5">Deleting the Git repository or production export; “retire” means disable the runtime and retain a documented, reversible archive.</li>
-    <li id="oos-6">Extracting a generic shared capture-queue skill or modifying the existing Capture-to-Inbox service; Runway capture remains deliberately dedicated.</li>
-  </ul>
-</details>
-
